.subckt MCR100_8 A G K
* MCR100-8 Sensitive Gate SCR
* A=Anode, G=Gate, K=Cathode
*
* Key specs modeled:
* - VDRM = 600V (MCR100-8)
* - IGT = 200µA (gate trigger current)
* - VGT = 0.8V (gate trigger voltage)
* - IH = 5mA (holding current)
* - VTM = 1.7V @ 1A (on-state voltage)
* - IT(RMS) = 0.8A max

* Two-transistor latch structure
Qpnp A n1 K Qpmod
Qnpn n1 n2 K Qnmod

* Gate resistor - sets IGT ~200µA
* VGT/IGT = 0.8V/200µA = 4kΩ
Rg G n2 500

* Gate-cathode shunt - sets holding current ~5mA
Rgk n2 K 4k

* Anode stability resistor - improves dv/dt behavior (20V/µs spec)
Rs n1 A 50k

* Gate protection diode (reverse gate voltage limit 5V)
Dgk K G Dgkmod

* PNP model - lower gain for realistic holding current
.model Qpmod PNP(
+ BF=15
+ IS=1e-13
+ ISE=1e-12
+ NE=1.5
+ BR=1
+ RC=0.5
+ RE=0.1
+ VAF=100
+ BV=600
+ IBV=100u
+ CJC=20p
+ CJE=30p
+ TF=100n
+ TR=1u)

* NPN model - higher gain, sensitive gate
.model Qnmod NPN(
+ BF=150
+ IS=1e-13
+ ISE=1e-12
+ NE=1.5
+ BR=1
+ RC=0.3
+ RE=0.05
+ VAF=100
+ BV=600
+ IBV=100u
+ CJC=15p
+ CJE=25p
+ TF=50n
+ TR=500n)

* Gate protection diode model
.model Dgkmod D(
+ IS=1e-14
+ BV=5
+ IBV=100u
+ RS=10)

.ends MCR100_8